<article class="env-lemma" id="0GY3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GY3">Lemma <span data-tag="0GY3">59.81.2</span>.</a> We have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  A[s, \frac{1}{\pi s + 1}] = \left(A[t, \frac{1}{\pi ^\ell t + 1}]\right)[s]/(\Phi (s) - t)  \]
</div>
  <p> In particular, the Hopf algebra of $G$ is a monogenic extension of the Hopf algebra of $H$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from the discussion above and the shape of $\Phi (s)$. In particular, note that using $\Phi (s) = t$ the element $\frac{1}{\pi ^\ell t + 1}$ becomes the element $\frac{1}{(\pi s + 1)^\ell }$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>